codex
Two material defects are now reproduced, despite the green submitted suite:

- the “no-replace” helper is check-then-rename; on POSIX a competing target created in that window is silently overwritten, defeating the stale/current-state defense used by rollback;
- staging a target beneath a missing parent creates that parent outside the journal, and a later rollback leaves the new empty directory behind instead of restoring the pre-transaction namespace.

I’m completing the evidence ledger and will route this as ordinary implementation rework (`to-dev`), not a stop-the-line blocker.
